Third-party components
----------------------

SecLab is built with third-party open-source software that is NOT covered by the
PolyForm Strict License and remains under its own terms. Those licenses continue
to apply to their respective components, and nothing in LICENSE overrides them.

The Rust dependency tree is permissively licensed (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD and
similar); an audit found no copyleft (GPL/AGPL) obligation in the dependencies
compiled into the shipping build. A full, machine-generated manifest of every
dependency and its license can be produced with `cargo about` (or `cargo
license`) and should accompany binary distributions.

Notable components and their own licenses:

  - nih-plug (CLAP plugin framework) ......................... ISC
  - egui / eframe (editor UI) ............................... MIT OR Apache-2.0
  - Rust standard crates (serde, etc.) ...................... MIT OR Apache-2.0

Plugin formats
--------------

SecLab exports to the CLAP format (first-party, via nih-plug's CLAP export).
VST3 and Audio Unit bundles are produced by clap-wrapper together with the
Steinberg VST3 SDK, which carry their own license terms (the VST3 SDK is dual
GPLv3 / Steinberg proprietary). "VST" is a trademark of Steinberg Media
Technologies GmbH; references to VST3/AU here name those formats only and claim
no affiliation or endorsement.
